## Context

Baseline integration tracker. The existing stock closes here; citation-chaining
additions, their merge and incremental screening belong to 1654. Final counting,
coverage reconciliation and the reproduction/freeze package belong to 1656.
See `docs/rel-corpus-completion-2026-10-08.md` and its measured baseline JSON.

Child of 0700. Design decision of 29 September: pool the raw pool and the search
results, then apply the ICF rule once to everything, instead of adding screened
works to a v2 corpus filtered otherwise. The six v2 filter flags stay as
information, not as a filter: of 489 works that the Southern search retrieved and
that the v2 filter had dropped, 122 are ICF after re-reading.

Work already done (ticket 1530, archive `~/data/projets/climate-finance-het/rel_sud/2026-09-29/`):
OpenAlex Southern search, screen of 25,693 works absent from the refined corpus,
Opus re-reading of 4,792 works, 55 sentinels. This work stays valid: same rule.

Chosen shape:
- append-only `icf_screen` table (work, stage, labeller and model, label, document type, country studied, reason, date), never in a regenerable file;
- REL view derived by join; `refined_works` stays pinned for the other deliverables;
- searches delivered as sources of the dedicated REL pool, with provenance and a per-delivery merge report (1730/1731); the catalogue and refined corpus for other deliverables stay pinned.

## Exit criteria
- [x] The searches (1530, 1650 to 1653) enter the dedicated REL pool as sources, with provenance and per-delivery merge reports (1730/1731; pinned catalogue remains an input, not overwritten; rebuilt on padme 2026-10-08)
- [x] Baseline pool screened under the dated ICF rule, with actual prompts, labellers/models and run provenance recorded (1733/1995; design-B threshold 0.90, Sol stage 2 and Fable/Opus corrections; 296 stage-2 and 59 title-less unscreened works are accepted residues)
- [~] Final sample audit of stage 2 by Fable — waived by author decision of 2026-10-07 (1733), not measured; historical agreement predates final corrections
- [x] Exit rule fixed for works left "uncertain" (177 to date): they remain ICF-eligible, flagged; final REL membership also applies seriousness and discipline (decision of 30 September 2026)
- [x] Baseline REL view rebuilt from pool, screen, dimensions and venue tables (1842/1843); 389,291 pool works, 7,499 fully graded included works / 7,484 observed families, including 5,354 research works / 5,339 families in the complete-year window; 5,894 no-abstract discipline-pending works reported separately; hashes and sensitivity in baseline evidence
- [x] Tested repository builders: corpus_rel_pool.py, corpus_icf_stage1_input.py and corpus_icf_stage2.py, with tests for deduplication, stage selection, chunks, imports and audit sampling (1731/1732). The 63 external actual-run/audit scripts and artifact map remain a 1656 packaging obligation, not a claim that all production scripts were committed
- [x] Counting unit for versions (working paper / article) fixed before the final view: the work family, published version as representative (decision of 30 September 2026)
